## Description
{: id="description" }

Chevin Technology designs and develops cutting-edge Ethernet protocol accelerators and Silicon Security Solutions for FPGA and ASIC platforms. Operating from our headquarters in Cambridge Science Park, UK, we deliver expert engineering and consulting services to clients in defense, aerospace, science, and telecommunications worldwide. Our unwavering commitment to providing robust, reliable, and efficient solutions ensures that our customers realize significant value from our innovations.

## CHERI Activities
{: id="cheri-activities" }

Chevin Technology was among the pioneering companies to participate in UKRI’s first cohort of Digital Security by Design Technology Access Programme, managed by Digital Catapult. Utilizing the CHERI technology and Morello hardware co-developed by the University of Cambridge and ARM, we explored how CHERI running on Morello could be integrated with our Silicon Security Solution, ChevinID, deployed on FPGA. This collaborative effort was aimed at evaluating the combined solution’s capability to protect memory with CHERI while delivering hardware authentication and software feature authorization through ChevinID.

## Description
{: id="description" }

Codasip is a processor technology company enabling system-on-chip developers to differentiate their products for competitive advantage. Customers leverage the transformational potential of the open RISC-V ISA in a unique way through Codasip’s Custom Compute offering: Codasip Studio design automation tools and a fully open architecture licensing model combine with a range of processor IP that can be easily customized. The company is proudly European and serves a global market, where billions of devices are already enabled by Codasip technology.

## CHERI Activities
{: id="cheri-activities" }

Codasip has added built-in, fine-grained memory protection to its RISC-V processors by extending the RISC-V ISA with CHERI-based custom instructions. The company announced the availability of CHERI in their 700 processor family in October 2023. This is the first commercial implementation of CHERI available for licensing. The company has committed to making CHERI available in all its new cores. As a founding member of RISC-V International, Codasip chair and actively contribute to several technical working groups, including security and safety topics of interest, and are active members in the CHERI Special Interest Group. In 2024, Codasip CHERI technology was awarded the prestigious Embedded Award at the Embedded World Conference in Nuremberg, Germany. In collaboration with other CHERI Alliance members, Codasip has built a CHERI SDK on existing open-source projects, and has donated it to the CHERI Alliance for unrestricted use by everyone implementing CHERI on RISC-V.

## CHERI Products
{: id="cheri-products" }

[https://codasip.com/solutions/riscv-processor-safety-security/cheri/](https://codasip.com/solutions/riscv-processor-safety-security/cheri/)

## Open-source Assets for CHERI
{: id="open-source-assets-for-cheri" }

[RISC-V Specification for CHERI Extensions – Draft (contributor)](https://github.com/riscv/riscv-cheri "https://github.com/riscv/riscv-cheri")

[CHERI RISC-V SDK](https://github.com/CHERI-Alliance "https://github.com/CHERI-Alliance")

## Description
{: id="description" }

The Critical Technologies Inc. (CTI) mission is trustworthy networked autonomy. CTI’s near term goal is to return meaningful control of devices, networks and data to their proper owners and enable a safe exit from the Red Queen’s race (of perpetually patching vulnerabilities due to undisciplined development). Our science fiction inspired long term optimistic vision is to lead a safe entry into a strong general AI/ML enabled Gaia protecting personal freedoms for all potential sophonts. CTI has diverse R&amp;D experience, from one of the first broadband cable modems for a commercial vendor in 1993, a massively parallel hardware real time neural network for DARPA in 1995, and resilient tactically deployed IP networks, to explainable AI/ML today.

## CHERI Activities
{: id="cheri-activities" }

CTI began promoting CHERI as part of a trustworthy whole-system stack at the 2019 RISC-V Summit and is working to integrate CHERI in open platforms for trustworthy networked autonomy.

